1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,437
This is Relay Home, a working
household planning prototype for the Alexa

2
00:00:04,437 --> 00:00:09,244
plus track. A school pickup changes, a
train runs late, and the whole

3
00:00:09,244 --> 00:00:13,682
evening needs a new plan. Everything
shown here uses synthetic household data.

4
00:00:13,682 --> 00:00:20,364
The web simulator calls a real, self hosted MCP
server over Streamable HTTP. It checks household context and

5
00:00:20,364 --> 00:00:26,675
previews an evening plan. Jo is approved and can
arrive fifteen minutes early. The pantry first dinner

6
00:00:26,675 --> 00:00:33,357
needs three dollars and twenty cents in additions. The
interface shows the actual tool calls and their timings.

7
00:00:33,357 --> 00:00:39,353
Now I ask for dinner under two dollars,
in twenty minutes. The planner switches to

8
00:00:39,353 --> 00:00:44,948
chickpea tomato soup, using only the demo
pantry. This is a constrained, deterministic planner,

9
00:00:44,948 --> 00:00:50,944
not a general language model. The MCP tools
also accept structured constraints from another client.

10
00:00:50,944 --> 00:00:56,051
Confirmation saves the local tasks and
shopping list. Pickup still needs the

11
00:00:56,051 --> 00:01:01,583
helper's acknowledgment. Relay has not sent a
message or bought anything. Revision checks,

12
00:01:01,583 --> 00:01:06,690
a ten minute expiry, and duplicate
protection prevent stale or repeated confirmation.

13
00:01:06,690 --> 00:01:12,929
After refreshing the page, the saved plan and
conversation are still here. Automated integration tests also

14
00:01:12,929 --> 00:01:18,779
stop and restart the server to verify that
this state survives beyond the browser session.

15
00:01:18,779 --> 00:01:23,851
Undo restores the previous local tasks,
preferences and shopping list, and records

16
00:01:23,851 --> 00:01:28,500
the change. The assistant cannot press
confirm on the user's behalf.

17
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:34,766
If Jo is unavailable, no approved helper can make
pickup on time. Relay explains the blocker and

18
00:01:34,766 --> 00:01:41,031
removes the confirm action. It does not substitute an
unapproved neighbor or pretend that pickup is covered.

19
00:01:41,031 --> 00:01:46,139
When Sam's meeting ends early, the old
preview becomes stale. Replanning finds that

20
00:01:46,139 --> 00:01:51,640
a parent can now make pickup. Relay
is locally runnable, with no paid API

21
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:56,748
or device required. This is an independent
simulation, not a live Alexa integration.

22
00:01:56,748 --> 00:02:02,407
If Sam cannot make pickup after the plan
is saved, the household owner records that

23
00:02:02,407 --> 00:02:07,689
response. Relay restores the local plan, excludes
Sam, and checks other approved helpers through

24
00:02:07,689 --> 00:02:13,348
MCP. Jo is proposed, but no message is
sent and the replacement still needs review.

25
00:02:13,348 --> 00:02:20,633
After a fresh page load, I ask what Relay
remembers. It identifies Jo as a current, unsaved pickup

26
00:02:20,633 --> 00:02:27,512
option, and separates that draft from earlier locally saved
changes. No real caregiver has acknowledged anything. The

27
00:02:27,512 --> 00:02:34,796
same context is available to an independent MCP client
after a server restart. Twenty four automated tests pass.
